	"descriptionMarkdown": "Note: This only works in Factorio 2.1. Without the ability to process signals based on which wire the signal is received on, it will not work.\n\nA book of what I am calling \"Auto Assembly Arrays\" that can process requests, block recipes when prerequisite items are running low, and swap fluid ingredients on a recipe switch. The \"Proof of Concept\" blueprint provides explanations for some of the more crucial components of the circuit. The other blueprints are what I consider to be the useful applications of this concept.\n\nThere is an issue that occurs inconsistently where the machine locks up, rapidly swapping between two recipes. I suspect this is a tick synchronization issue due to modifying the requests while the machine is running, but it only occurs rarely, so I have been unsuccessful in diagnosing that issue.",
